Debug mode leaves a `## Not a heading` line inside a fenced code block unhighlighted, since it isn't a heading, and highlights the two real headings.
== args
--debug
input/fences.md
== file input/fences.md
# Overview

```md
## Not a heading
```

## Real heading
== stdout
«# Overview»

```md
## Not a heading
```

«## Real heading»
== stderr
== exit 0
